{"title":"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An unusual die has the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/d/81d76a21cfe8e6f400692384caea6f5b1066b78c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 2, 3, 3, 5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on its six faces. Two of these dice are rolled. The two numbers on the top faces are added. How many different sums are possible?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/5/b458ee0bf98c795dcda62b5569fd2264ed043a25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 6 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 7 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 8 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 9 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The unique numbers on the die are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/3/ff3e93cc98d2eaa04bec7bea0273c471161b4570.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 3, 5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>If the first number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then the possible sums are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/e/d9e6fe0d6361344356eb49dcd71a550c665faac2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/27803b32e1de1532968c2bc198dd16b640f3e4b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 3 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cda1a27fa2e448ac727bb0425727c1e5b22bb6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 5 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/2/9529894c79f8ce82b52a23a8779ab4ebb2c2901a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 8 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sums.\n</p><p>If the first number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then the possible sums that we haven't got so far are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/1/0e1a7f4874925e5df19990fe6f922b0cb3181907.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 3 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/108880936ebf093c88308f58baa4abe040466366.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 5 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/0/d00837fc2e7e6e6fec56fb950e0caef46dd54cb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 8 = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/3/893159a18d02e3488bd47dc581c936df62f66cb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> excluded because it is the same as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/2/862d4aa8a195ae71a271f6e061af41aa1d4e6e8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />). There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sums.\n</p><p>If the first number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then the possible sums that we haven't got so far are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/d/e2db1f00de266bd67fdc8a4b82718454e40a7ebe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 5 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/4/0f415cda52590a9ebab71db39b7caea485ad25ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 8 = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />. However, we already have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so there is only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sum.\n</p><p>If the first number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then there is only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sum that we haven't got so far: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/2/232baead1207f7962d526e6375fe2f0828d3fbc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 + 8 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f278703365183ea879a76ce310e218c4e04f66f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + 3 + 1 + 1 = 7 + 2 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(D) } 9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"250\" height=\"30\" /> possible sums.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal\">2006 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/P